# Machine-local paths and devices, copied to .env.local (which is gitignored).
#
#     cp .env.local.example .env.local     # PowerShell: copy .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Every value is optional. Anything left commented out is either auto-detected
# or taken from the environment `idf.py`'s export script already set, so on a
# machine with a normal ESP-IDF install this file can stay empty. Set a key
# only when the guess is wrong.
#
# Format is KEY=value, one per line, `#` for comments. Forward slashes work on
# Windows too, and quotes around a value are optional (needed only for a path
# with spaces in it).

# --- ESP-IDF -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the IDF is checked out and where its toolchains live. Both are exported
# by IDF's own export.ps1/export.sh, so you only need them here if you run the
# scripts from a shell that has not been through that - IDF_PATH in particular
# is what neos/main/idf_component.yml resolves its usb component override
# against, and the firmware will not configure without it.
#IDF_PATH=C:/ESP-IDF/esp-idf/v5.4.2/esp-idf
#IDF_TOOLS_PATH=C:/ESP-IDF/.espressif

# The interpreter ./do runs the python scripts with. Only needed when the
# search (IDF_PYTHON_ENV_PATH, then the venvs under IDF_TOOLS_PATH, then a
# python on PATH with pyserial) finds nothing or finds the wrong one.
#NEOS_PYTHON=C:/ESP-IDF/.espressif/python_env/idf5.4_py3.11_env/Scripts/python.exe

# esptool, for scripts/restore-flash. Found next to the IDF python otherwise.
#ESPTOOL=C:/ESP-IDF/.espressif/python_env/idf5.4_py3.11_env/Scripts/esptool.exe

# --- the tablet --------------------------------------------------------------
# The Tab5's serial port. Auto-detected from the ESP32-P4's own USB-Serial-JTAG
# device (VID 303A), so this is only for a machine with two boards plugged in.
# COM16 on Windows, /dev/ttyACM0 on Linux, /dev/cu.usbmodem* on macOS.
#NEOS_PORT=COM16

# Drive or mount point of the SD card reader, for scripts/deploy-card.ps1.
#NEOS_CARD_DRIVE=H:
